# ---- STUDENT TODO 3: joint limit check (SHACL-SPARQL) -----------------------
# Write a sh:NodeShape targeted at soma:JointState that reports every joint
# angle lying outside its own joint's limits.
#   - The angle is on the JointState:      soma:hasJointPosition
#   - The state links to its joint via:    hw3:isStateOfJoint
#   - The joint carries its limits as:     hw3:hasJointLowerLimit / hw3:hasJointUpperLimit
# SHACL Core cannot compare two values taken from DIFFERENT nodes, so use a
# SHACL-SPARQL constraint: sh:sparql [ sh:message ... ; sh:prefixes
# hw3:SparqlPrefixes ; sh:select """ SELECT $this WHERE { ... FILTER (...) } """ ].
# Rules:
#   - On violation, sh:message must begin with "JOINT_LIMIT_VIOLATION:".
#   - Limits are INCLUSIVE: an angle exactly equal to a limit is legal
#     (the TA dataset contains such a boundary record), so the FILTER must
#     use strict comparisons (< lower, > upper).
# The prefixes declaration below is provided for you — reference it with
# sh:prefixes hw3:SparqlPrefixes inside your constraint.
hw3:SparqlPrefixes sh:declare
    [ sh:prefix "hw3" ;  sh:namespace "http://taica.course/hw3/ontology#"^^xsd:anyURI ] ,
    [ sh:prefix "soma" ; sh:namespace "http://www.ease-crc.org/ont/SOMA.owl#"^^xsd:anyURI ] .

